  "goodToKnow": "Der Amtsträger (die Amtsträgerin) is an office holder or official: politicians, civil servants, judges, also church office holders. In criminal law, Amtsträger is a defined term, and bribing them (Bestechung) is punished severely. Politicians in office must respect a Neutralitätsgebot when acting officially. Das Amt is office or authority. The plural is the same."
